# Copy to .env.local and fill in real values. This documents the config the
# app needs as the mock-data/localStorage service layer
# (src/modules/<domain>/*Service.js, src/services/*.js) is swapped for the
# real backend (see docs/ENGINEERING_BLUEPRINT.md, backend/).
#
# Hosting: Cloudflare Pages (frontend, this repo) + Cloudflare Workers (backend
# API, translation, auth) — see wrangler.toml. Cloudflare account credentials
# (API token, account ID) are deploy-time secrets in CI/the Workers project's
# own wrangler config, NOT client-side REACT_APP_* vars — a token prefixed
# REACT_APP_ ships inside the browser bundle, which would leak it publicly.

# Base URL for the Cloudflare Workers backend API (backend/, see its README).
# Read by src/modules/auth/authService.js once REACT_APP_API_BASE_URL is set
# AND src/config/featureFlags.js's `realAuthApi` flag is turned on — until
# both are true, authService keeps using its localStorage mock unchanged.
REACT_APP_API_BASE_URL=
